      "title": "About this workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Depth, normals, semantic identity and motion tracking\n\nThe frozen foundation models inside CorridorKey 2.0, exposed as their own tools:\n\n- **Depth & Normals** (MoGe-2): clip-consistent depth and surface orientation. `geometry` works with the core MoGe nodes (Render MoGe Geometry, Convert MoGe Point Map to Mesh).\n- **Semantic Identity** (C-RADIOv4): a stable feature-colour video, and with a reference mask a per-frame mask of the same subject.\n- **Motion Tracking** (RVM): identity features, motion energy, and a reference mask carried through the clip.\n\nHere the tracked mask is fed back into the keyer as a per-frame hint (rough matte quality).\n\n**Your footage:** replace **Demo Clip** with **Load Video → Get Video Components** (or an image sequence loader) and connect its `images`. The Demo Clip is a synthetic green-screen shot with its exact matte, so every example runs without media. Paint the reference mask on one frame and set `reference_frame`."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Depth, normals, semantic identity and motion tracking\n\nThe frozen foundation models inside CorridorKey 2.0, exposed as their own tools:\n\n- **Depth & Normals** (MoGe-2): clip-consistent depth and surface orientation. `geometry` works with the core MoGe nodes (Render MoGe Geometry, Convert MoGe Point Map to Mesh).\n- **Semantic Identity** (C-RADIOv4): a stable feature-colour video, and with a reference mask a per-frame mask of the same subject.\n- **Motion Tracking** (RVM): identity features, motion energy, and a reference mask carried through the clip.\n\nHere the tracked mask is fed back into the keyer as a per-frame hint (rough matte quality).\n\n**Your footage:** replace **Demo Clip** with **Load Video → Get Video Components** (or an image sequence loader) and connect its `images`. The Demo Clip is a synthetic green-screen shot with its exact matte, so every example runs without media. Paint the reference mask on one frame and set `reference_frame`."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
